{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791819865,"nonce":"MpOjWXq7nEIMZ/DD3mEkXjQk72E=","message":"The severe CI slowdown is caused by losing the declared array element type at literal initialization, not by treating an inference variable as a declared generic. The earlier inference-variable guard did not improve the benchmark and was removed.\n\nNBody.bodies is Array\u003cBody\u003e, but its factory-call literal carries an inferred Array\u003cDynamic\u003e type. Lowering the assignment using that literal type sets BOXED_ELEMS while storing raw Body pointers. Every lookup then enters haxe_array_get_typed and reference unboxing. The correction lowers literals against their destination array type and converts Dynamic element expressions to concrete slot payloads once during initialization. Inferred mixed literals retain their original path.\n\nOfficial benchmark runner, 15 warmups and 10 measured iterations, compilation excluded:\nMac v65: tiered 544.211ms (540.047-604.444), LLVM 562.481ms (543.409-892.594), Cranelift 703.627ms (698.180-708.334).\nNUC v65: LLVM 389.220ms, tiered 410.963ms, Cranelift 456.097ms.\nIdle NUC comparison: exact downloaded CI build 38250293216 tiered 3958.459ms (3913.408-4054.594), corrected frozen v65 tiered 391.527ms (385.070-405.703). Only build-time source-path strings in the downloaded executable were relocated to the existing checkout; benchmark code and workload were unchanged.\n\nThe first broad element-conversion candidate lost Issue10482, Issue3799 and TestReflect. Restricting conversion to destination-driven literal lowering recovered all three. Mac v66 full conformance: 1083/1092, no rows gained or lost versus v64. The final candidate additionally preserves pointer representation for boxed nullable Float/Bool array reads; validation is underway.\n\nThese execution-only timings supersede the earlier end-to-end CLI timings. The Mac tiered and LLVM medians meet the requested sub-600ms execution target. CI has not yet rerun the corrected source; the older small performance drift against hxcpp remains unverified there.","files":null}]}